## 10. Known Quirks / Watch-outs

> [!WARNING]
> **AWS Personalize is currently DISABLED.** `scheduler.py` line 32: `self.training_enabled = False` — comment says "Using AWS Personalize batch inference instead" but the aws_personalize module is also present. The system currently runs **fully local ML** via `local_ml_pipeline.py`.

> [!NOTE]
> **Dual deployment modes** — The Procfile (Heroku) and deploy_full_stack.sh (on-premise) are both maintained. The `.env` detection logic auto-sets `PG_SSLMODE=require` for Heroku and `prefer` for local.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **unified_customer_id** is synthesized as `{phone}_{first_name_lower}` — not a stable UUID. This can cause issues if customer phone numbers or names change between orders.

> [!CAUTION]
> **offline_ tables are TRUNCATED daily** — `TRUNCATE TABLE offline_user_recommendations` before every batch insert. If the pipeline fails mid-run, recommendation serving will fall back to real-time SQL queries (which is acceptable but slower).
